WEBVTT

00:07.830 --> 00:09.580
Wow, it's the ocean...

00:10.000 --> 00:11.790
It is the ocean, isn't it?

00:12.080 --> 00:17.670
As expected, when there is a lot of nature around,
that refreshing feeling is something else, you know?

00:18.630 --> 00:21.330
Plus, the smell of the ocean is nice.

00:21.330 --> 00:23.960
Although when it is the windy season, there is salty
air, so hair care is a little difficult.

00:24.330 --> 00:25.380
I see.

00:25.670 --> 00:28.040
But are you really sure today was okay for you?

00:28.540 --> 00:31.170
Yes. It is a "special outing."

00:31.420 --> 00:33.420
Well, I suppose so.

00:33.670 --> 00:34.380
Whoa!

00:41.460 --> 00:44.040
Wow! So, you are using it.

00:44.420 --> 00:45.420
Of course.

00:45.830 --> 00:49.000
I mean, after all, Sasaki-san,
this is a present that you gave me.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.290
That makes me happy.

00:50.540 --> 00:53.040
You see, Sajo-san, I chose it
based off my impression of you.

00:55.580 --> 00:56.960
Is that so...

01:11.080 --> 01:15.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

01:11.080 --> 01:15.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

01:15.170 --> 01:20.750
With a command from the sky that's peeking out,
we hold onto our feelings as we depart

01:20.750 --> 01:25.460
Even though our eyes meet,
we're swayed by the wind into a roundabout way

01:26.540 --> 01:32.000
A dream snapshot taken by the blink of the eyes;
the memories adorn my heart

01:32.000 --> 01:37.420
It seems I like these times; even though they're frustrating

01:38.460 --> 01:43.330
Staying away then getting closer; a dream I'd started to give up on

01:43.580 --> 01:49.040
The day I can land that well; I want to try chasing after that

01:49.040 --> 01:54.460
The sky is filled up with the things that can't be all conveyed

01:54.630 --> 02:00.250
For some reason, the change in countenance
of your true feelings was at odds

02:00.250 --> 02:08.540
Even though I might get lost, the sky always had two heartbeats

02:08.540 --> 02:11.040
I've told you many times

02:11.210 --> 02:17.210
If these youthful feelings are joined together,
I wonder what kind of view will spread out

02:17.210 --> 02:21.880
I want to know that colorful feeling

02:28.790 --> 02:31.830
<b>You Know, Female College Students are Seriously Amazing</b>

02:29.000 --> 02:31.580
"This year's recommendation," huh?
But having said that...

02:32.170 --> 02:33.130
<b>Bookstore Staff's Choice</b>

02:32.170 --> 02:33.130
<b>This year's recommendation</b>

02:32.170 --> 02:33.130
<b>The one book I recommend is...</b>

02:32.500 --> 02:34.460
Sajo-san. Hello.

02:34.460 --> 02:35.170
Whoa!

02:35.420 --> 02:38.540
Welcome, Sasaki-san.
Are you headed to the campus today?

02:38.540 --> 02:43.790
No, I am on my way to the library,
but I wanted to chat, so I ended up stopping by.

02:43.920 --> 02:47.920
Seriously? Sasaki-san, since
you come over often, it is comforting.

02:49.330 --> 02:52.790
Wow, that is stylish. Sasaki-san,
you put on things like that.

02:54.630 --> 02:56.920
Although this was because I was influenced by friends.

02:56.920 --> 02:59.630
I went with my dad to go make this just a while ago.

02:59.630 --> 03:01.040
What? It's handmade?

03:01.630 --> 03:04.210
Hang on, a female college student,
on good terms with her dad?

03:04.580 --> 03:08.460
I mean, by the time Big Sis was an elementary schooler,
she separated her laundry from my old man's.

03:08.710 --> 03:09.630
Sajo-san?

03:10.630 --> 03:13.330
Oh, I mean, I was thinking that you are skillful.

03:13.790 --> 03:17.380
There is a seaside store that will
teach you how, while you make them.

03:17.540 --> 03:19.250
Wow, that sounds nice.

03:19.630 --> 03:21.040
What is the store called?

03:23.290 --> 03:25.250
Oh, let's see...

03:26.380 --> 03:27.710
Oh! Whoa...

03:28.000 --> 03:29.330
Oh, this is it!

03:29.500 --> 03:32.500
<b>Craft Shop</b>

03:29.750 --> 03:34.380
A pretty young woman runs the store by herself.
Sajo-san, probably to your liking.

03:34.460 --> 03:37.130
What!? Does it appear that I like young women that...

03:37.670 --> 03:40.500
I was thinking that you like stores
that are privately owned, so...

03:40.670 --> 03:42.880
Oh, yeah! I think I do like them.

03:44.580 --> 03:47.670
From here, it would be a train and a bus, huh?

03:48.210 --> 03:49.630
Are you going to go there?

03:49.920 --> 03:53.830
What? Yes. Plus, things like handmade crafts are stylish.

03:54.080 --> 03:54.920
Also...

03:55.420 --> 03:56.250
"Also"?

03:59.000 --> 04:01.460
It seems like you can make them
to one's own preference too.

04:02.330 --> 04:06.460
It's Natsukawa's birthday soon.
What would be good for this year?

04:06.460 --> 04:10.080
In the first place, should I even give a gift?
I've been thinking about this for a long time, but...

04:10.750 --> 04:12.540
You can make something like this too, huh...?

04:14.500 --> 04:16.290
Um, Sasaki-san?

04:19.670 --> 04:21.670
Would you like to go with me?

04:22.670 --> 04:28.290
Therefore, unexpectedly, that's why I ended up on
a special outing with a female college student, but...

04:28.670 --> 04:31.250
Is this like, what one would call,
a female college student's composure?

04:31.710 --> 04:35.790
It doesn't seem like she feels there is any special
meaning to going on an outing with just me.

04:37.330 --> 04:38.380
Oh. Sasaki-san?

04:38.380 --> 04:38.960
Oh!

04:38.960 --> 04:42.790
Oh, you see... When I think that
I might be seen by someone...

04:43.250 --> 04:43.920
What?

04:44.420 --> 04:48.330
Oh, like you would be embarrassed if it was regarded
like you and I were a couple, kind of thing?

04:48.540 --> 04:49.500
My clothes...

04:49.830 --> 04:51.080
What? Your clothes?

04:51.670 --> 04:54.580
As usual, you have that sense of being
like a lovely young woman, you know?

04:54.920 --> 04:56.580
Th-that isn't what I meant...

04:56.960 --> 05:01.210
Actually, you see, this kind of outfit is used
for when I go out to see you, Sajo-san,

05:01.210 --> 05:03.960
or like at times when I won't see anyone from school.

05:04.420 --> 05:07.040
Huh? What kind of outfits are you usually in?

05:07.250 --> 05:11.380
Normally, well... The ones from when
I was an elementary school student...

05:11.710 --> 05:12.210
Huh?

05:12.710 --> 05:13.380
Huh!?

05:13.630 --> 05:14.420
Huh!?

05:15.420 --> 05:18.460
Hang on, can she really fit into clothes
from when she was an elementary schooler!?

05:18.830 --> 05:21.750
D-don't your friends say anything about that?

05:21.750 --> 05:23.580
Like, that you should change into something else?

05:23.580 --> 05:27.500
What? How do you know? I get told that by everyone.

05:28.080 --> 05:30.710
Although they are my favorites because they are cute.

05:30.710 --> 05:35.580
Well... How do I say this? I guess that sounds fine
if you are using them as house clothes.

05:35.790 --> 05:37.750
Yes, I suppose so...

05:38.130 --> 05:42.500
Oh, but I think it is wonderful that
you take good care of your things for a long time.

05:42.790 --> 05:43.460
Oh!

05:44.580 --> 05:46.130
Thank you very much!

05:46.380 --> 05:48.130
<b>Aichi, I've arrived at the meeting place.</b>

05:46.380 --> 05:48.130
<b>I think we should almost be there.</b>

05:46.380 --> 05:48.130
<b>Okay.</b>

05:47.330 --> 05:48.130
Kei!

05:48.630 --> 05:49.330
Hey!

05:50.290 --> 05:54.000
Sorry. I was packing Airi's change of clothes,
and we ended up being late.

05:54.170 --> 05:55.420
That's okay.

05:55.420 --> 05:57.250
Wow! It's Ai-chan!

06:01.880 --> 06:04.330
Kei, what do you have in there?

06:04.580 --> 06:07.880
Huh? If we're going to the ocean,
then there are various things we need, right?

06:08.080 --> 06:09.580
Speaking of, what about you, Aichi?

06:10.250 --> 06:12.710
For the most part, it's Airi's stuff, but...

06:13.750 --> 06:14.420
Oh!

06:14.710 --> 06:16.580
Isn't this Sajotchi's house?

06:17.290 --> 06:21.500
Sajotchi's in luck. Because he's going
to be able to see Aichi in a swimsuit.

06:21.500 --> 06:23.460
What!? We're inviting him too!?

06:23.460 --> 06:26.790
Yeah. Let's give him the duty
of being the bag-carrier.

06:26.960 --> 06:29.580
B-but I don't know, since this is so sudden.

06:30.630 --> 06:32.170
Huh? Is he at his part-time job?

06:32.790 --> 06:35.250
I had thought he'd be free, doing nothing after all, but...

06:35.250 --> 06:37.630
I'm going to the ocean with Kei-chan!

06:37.630 --> 06:40.330
We're going to the ocean! C'mon, Ai-chan!

06:40.500 --> 06:41.460
Yay!

06:44.790 --> 06:48.790
Given it is a beautiful white beach, it is called
"Mishirohama." That was well-put, you know?

06:49.630 --> 06:50.960
That is true.

06:52.880 --> 06:56.290
When female college students go on dates,
do they go out for long drives, or stuff like that?

07:01.130 --> 07:05.460
Oh, by any chance, are you looking for
beautiful young women clad in swimsuits?

07:05.460 --> 07:06.790
You shouldn't, you know.

07:06.790 --> 07:09.710
What!? Th-there is no way I would be, you know!?

07:09.830 --> 07:12.540
It's just that I was thinking, "Was the ocean this pretty?"

07:13.380 --> 07:16.460
Well, Sajo-san, you were saying it had been a long time.

07:16.460 --> 07:20.880
First time in several years.
Sasaki-san, do you come to the ocean a lot?

07:21.130 --> 07:25.170
Yes. Last year too, with my family.
Although I haven't swam in it this year.

07:25.670 --> 07:29.290
I also went when I was in middle school,
to hang out with my friends, and that's it.

07:29.630 --> 07:34.460
It is kind of like that for me too. It is also tough
that I have to buy a swimsuit every year.

07:34.460 --> 07:36.500
What? You don't wear the one from last year?

07:37.040 --> 07:37.750
Oh!

07:38.040 --> 07:39.500
It doesn't fit...

07:39.750 --> 07:40.750
Sajo-san?

07:41.170 --> 07:43.920
Oh, yes. Let's see, from here, it is...

07:43.920 --> 07:47.250
It is that way. I remember how to get there,
so I will show you the way.

07:47.250 --> 07:50.380
Oh, seriously? I will be counting on you-

07:52.250 --> 07:53.830
I-Illicit sexual relations with a minor!

07:54.210 --> 07:55.580
S..Sasaki-san!

07:55.580 --> 07:56.210
Huh?

07:56.500 --> 07:58.830
Oh! I-I am sorry! It's just out of habit...

07:59.250 --> 08:00.380
My apologies.

08:00.540 --> 08:02.670
Oh, not at all. Nothing to apologize for.

08:02.960 --> 08:04.420
Well, shall we go?

08:05.250 --> 08:06.130
Yes...

08:08.500 --> 08:10.250
Are you okay with the footing there?

08:10.420 --> 08:11.670
They're platforms, so...

08:12.040 --> 08:13.250
Let's go slowly.

08:13.540 --> 08:14.920
Thank you very much.

08:15.170 --> 08:16.170
Alright!

08:16.500 --> 08:17.040
Hup!

08:17.290 --> 08:18.710
Hup! Whoa, Whoa! Whoa!

08:19.040 --> 08:21.420
Hup! Whoa! Hup!

08:22.040 --> 08:24.130
You know, female college students
are seriously amazing.

08:26.630 --> 08:29.670
So, this is it. I am kind of getting nervous...

08:29.920 --> 08:34.750
It will be fine. I have come here
before, so... Let us go inside.

08:35.130 --> 08:36.290
Oh, yes.

08:38.250 --> 08:39.250
Wow...

08:40.500 --> 08:42.250
Am I the only guy?

08:43.500 --> 08:45.330
That makes me even more nervous, though...

08:46.380 --> 08:47.670
Welcome!

08:48.000 --> 08:49.830
Oh? You're...

08:50.710 --> 08:52.460
Oh, yes! I came here before too.

08:52.460 --> 08:56.670
That's right. You left a strong impression
because you seem like a very mature girl.

08:57.330 --> 08:58.580
Is that so?

08:58.960 --> 09:00.420
Are you here with your boyfriend today?

09:00.420 --> 09:00.830
Oh!

09:01.080 --> 09:03.710
Huh!? Oh, um... Well, he's...

09:04.040 --> 09:06.880
Oh, it's not that kind of relationship in particular.

09:06.880 --> 09:08.290
Oh, is that so?

09:09.500 --> 09:12.420
What is this? Is it girl talk between
a female office worker and female college student?

09:09.830 --> 09:11.170
Take your time looking around.

09:11.170 --> 09:11.960
Okay.

09:12.540 --> 09:14.880
This is making me think I'm like a really young boy.

09:15.580 --> 09:19.580
<b>Amazonite &</b>

09:15.580 --> 09:19.580
<b>Turquoise Bracelet</b>

09:15.590 --> 09:19.580
<b>Inca Rose & Rose</b>

09:15.590 --> 09:19.580
<b>Quartz Bracelet</b>

09:15.590 --> 09:19.580
<b>Suede Cord</b>

09:15.590 --> 09:19.580
<b>(Leather string)</b>

09:15.590 --> 09:19.580
<b>& Tassel Charm</b>

09:16.000 --> 09:18.250
Wow, amazing. Shall we look around here?

09:18.250 --> 09:19.380
Yes, sure.

09:20.040 --> 09:21.080
Wow!

09:21.330 --> 09:24.080
<b>These are the</b>

09:21.330 --> 09:24.080
<b>most popular.</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>How about making</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>a bracelet that's</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>prefect for you?</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>Bracelet parts</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>Semi-precious</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:24.080
<b>stones & shells.</b>

09:21.790 --> 09:23.920
Are these the raw materials over here, maybe?

09:24.460 --> 09:25.420
This is...

09:25.630 --> 09:27.380
It has been halved.

09:28.040 --> 09:30.130
That is a part of a pearl shell.

09:30.580 --> 09:32.380
Are these ones that were broken?

09:32.380 --> 09:38.130
No, they've been cut into small pieces so that
they're easier to work with, as shells are very hard.

09:38.750 --> 09:40.960
Is it like where you use a file or something like that?

09:41.080 --> 09:45.000
Yes. However, if it was just something like sandpaper,

09:45.330 --> 09:47.380
then they're no match for them,
so a file that contains diamonds is used.

09:47.380 --> 09:47.960
What!?

09:48.460 --> 09:49.630
How do I put this...?

09:49.830 --> 09:54.670
I was thinking it was kind of like how you
make stamps in class. Am I gonna be okay?

09:54.670 --> 09:56.460
Huh? Sajo-san?

09:56.880 --> 09:58.460
Huh!? Oh, I mean...

09:58.460 --> 09:59.460
This is...

09:59.710 --> 10:02.210
Wow! That is really pretty.

10:02.420 --> 10:06.170
That's a paua shell.
Those are obtained from New Zealand.

10:06.460 --> 10:07.710
Do you like this kind of shell?

10:07.710 --> 10:10.130
Well, it's not that I like them, but...

10:10.130 --> 10:12.750
Sajo-san, should we make something?

10:12.750 --> 10:14.540
Body Touching Alarm issued!

10:14.920 --> 10:16.670
Well, we're already here, after all.

10:17.040 --> 10:19.830
We came all this way, and to just buy something
and go home is, well, you know?

10:20.460 --> 10:21.500
Alright!

10:21.880 --> 10:23.880
Sasaki-san, what kind of thing are you going to make?

10:24.040 --> 10:29.630
Well, last time I combined
small shells to make a bracelet, but...

10:29.630 --> 10:32.040
This time, I would like to make a necklace.

10:32.040 --> 10:33.330
That sounds good.

10:33.790 --> 10:35.040
And you, Sajo-san?

10:35.500 --> 10:39.750
Oh, well... I still only have kind of a fuzzy idea, but...

10:40.130 --> 10:43.380
In that case, it would be better if you decide
on what you want to make beforehand.

10:43.920 --> 10:46.670
It'll end up being difficult if you go ahead
and break apart or shave off things.

10:47.000 --> 10:48.210
I see.

10:48.790 --> 10:49.830
That's true...

10:50.210 --> 10:54.580
Since I'm gifting it to Natsukawa, I'd like to
make it something that suits her as much as possible.

10:56.380 --> 10:59.790
I apologize if I have the wrong idea, but is this a gift?

10:59.790 --> 11:00.420
What!?

11:00.630 --> 11:04.670
The way you look as you're thinking is serious,
so I thought maybe that's it.

11:05.000 --> 11:06.330
Is that true?

11:06.580 --> 11:10.170
Well, yes. An acquaintance
of mine has a birthday soon.

11:10.540 --> 11:11.670
Of the opposite sex?

11:11.670 --> 11:13.040
You mean it is for a girl!?

11:13.380 --> 11:18.670
Oh, yes. That is why I was thinking if I could make
some kind of accessory or pretty ornament.

11:15.790 --> 11:16.580
Wow...

11:18.670 --> 11:20.880
Yeah, uh-huh. He's a boy.

11:21.250 --> 11:22.790
He is a boy, isn't he?

11:22.790 --> 11:23.630
Okay...

11:24.210 --> 11:27.460
If you're going to make something,
then you'll be choosing from the materials that are here.

11:27.880 --> 11:29.540
Is there something that catches your eye?

11:31.420 --> 11:34.540
Oh! I will choose this. It is cute!

11:34.880 --> 11:36.420
That's a juvenile shell.

11:36.960 --> 11:38.170
Pink, huh...?

11:38.790 --> 11:40.540
That might look good on Natsukawa too.

11:42.750 --> 11:48.290
No, pink is a no-go. I'd die.
Plus, it's doesn't quite fit Natsukawa's image.

11:48.670 --> 11:51.380
The one that would bring out
Natsukawa's good features would be...?

11:52.170 --> 11:57.540
By any chance, is this like someone you like?
The person whose birthday is coming up soon.

11:57.540 --> 12:01.330
What? Sasaki-san, I guess for you,
you can see right through me, huh?

12:01.750 --> 12:06.710
Your girlfriend will be delighted, that she will
receive a handmade accessory for her birthday.

12:06.710 --> 12:11.460
Oh, she isn't my girlfriend. She doesn't
want to do stuff like be in a relationship.

12:11.460 --> 12:12.130
What?

12:12.540 --> 12:13.920
I like her, but...

12:14.130 --> 12:15.710
It's my unrequited love.

12:16.040 --> 12:17.580
I see...

12:18.580 --> 12:22.330
But if you aren't thinking that
you want to go out with her, then why?

12:22.790 --> 12:25.790
Ah... It's not as if my crush itself
has ended or anything like that.

12:26.750 --> 12:29.580
My feelings of love for that person
haven't gone away, so...

12:29.920 --> 12:31.290
Stop following me!

12:31.830 --> 12:34.210
I fell in love with Natsukawa and then I got rejected.

12:34.630 --> 12:37.420
I may no longer do something
like approach her anymore.

12:38.380 --> 12:42.670
But, having said that, it wasn't two and a half years
where nothing was gained by it.

12:43.670 --> 12:45.540
I was able to do better at studying, and...

12:45.960 --> 12:47.540
If I hadn't fallen in love with Natsukawa,

12:47.540 --> 12:50.380
then I also don't think I would've done
something like "self-improvement."

12:51.250 --> 12:53.710
So, this is for my self-satisfaction.

12:54.420 --> 12:57.420
The birthday will become an excuse
for me to give a present to that person.

12:57.750 --> 13:01.710
And if that person smiles, then lucky me, I guess.

13:03.330 --> 13:07.670
There is no one who would not be happy
to receive something from someone, you know?

13:08.000 --> 13:09.330
You think so?

13:09.540 --> 13:11.710
Yes. That is what I think.

13:12.380 --> 13:15.540
Sorry to bother you while you're talking. How's it going?

13:15.540 --> 13:17.460
Oh. I'm sorry, I still haven't...

13:19.040 --> 13:23.210
No. It's fine that I give Natsukawa
what I think would suit her.

13:23.710 --> 13:25.420
Even if it ends up that she doesn't like it.

13:25.670 --> 13:29.420
To be able to give Natsukawa a gift;
that is what's important.

13:30.080 --> 13:33.080
Um, instead of the one from earlier,
is there a lighter colored...?

13:37.040 --> 13:41.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

13:37.040 --> 13:41.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

13:44.290 --> 13:46.170
There! Pass to you, Ai-chan!

13:50.330 --> 13:51.540
I got it!

13:51.540 --> 13:54.080
Alright! Next up is a race to the ocean!

13:54.080 --> 13:55.040
Yay!

14:01.920 --> 14:04.040
Ai-chan, good job! Well done!

14:05.710 --> 14:06.670
Good job!

14:11.250 --> 14:12.790
I'm exhausted!

14:13.130 --> 14:16.460
Sorry about that. And this is a precious
day off from your club activities.

14:16.460 --> 14:18.830
Well, I like being physically active.

14:19.500 --> 14:23.380
Aichi, you're the one who was attending to her
this whole time up until just now, so you take a rest.

14:23.380 --> 14:24.080
Huh?

14:24.630 --> 14:25.330
Oh!

14:25.710 --> 14:27.170
What a stylish store...

14:27.170 --> 14:29.330
Doesn't it say, "Craft Shop"?

14:29.830 --> 14:32.330
Oh! Wanna make something as a memento of today?

14:32.710 --> 14:33.830
Wanna make!

14:34.420 --> 14:35.960
Should we take a quick look?

14:37.130 --> 14:39.170
That's the kind of image I want to make it into, but...

14:40.580 --> 14:41.330
Huh?

14:45.580 --> 14:47.960
Sasaki-san, do you have a younger sister?

14:47.960 --> 14:48.580
What?

14:48.830 --> 14:52.380
Oh, this is from the time I came with my dad recently.

14:53.460 --> 14:56.380
Sasaki-san, do you have a hobby of cosplaying?

14:57.170 --> 14:58.710
Oh please, Sajo-san.

14:59.130 --> 15:01.880
That is the uniform for my middle school.

15:02.420 --> 15:03.460
Excuse me?

15:12.920 --> 15:15.710
Sorry about that. There weren't
any that were already cut up.

15:15.710 --> 15:18.460
Oh no, this is just my self-indulgence, so...

15:19.000 --> 15:21.330
Just what in the world is going on!?

15:24.080 --> 15:26.830
The one that is closest in color to what you want
would be this one.

15:27.880 --> 15:29.580
So, I'll be cutting this then...

15:30.420 --> 15:31.630
It's a pretty color...

15:32.790 --> 15:36.210
I am currently cutting a hard abalone shell.

15:36.830 --> 15:38.750
Hang on, that's not what's at issue, but-

15:38.750 --> 15:40.130
You can do it! You can do it!

15:40.330 --> 15:42.960
You can do it! You can do it! You can do it!

15:42.960 --> 15:46.670
How can it be, that this is a middle school girl!?

15:47.000 --> 15:49.040
Whoa!

15:49.040 --> 15:51.420
Wow! Sajo-san is fired up!

15:49.250 --> 15:50.750
I'm gonna do this!

15:51.580 --> 15:52.380
Yeah!

15:52.540 --> 15:54.330
I don't have a choice but to get fired up.

15:54.330 --> 15:58.130
Because I don't know where
I'm supposed to vent this bewilderment at!

15:58.580 --> 16:02.000
I am Fuka Sasaki, a 3rd-year
at Mishirohama Girls' Middle School.

16:02.290 --> 16:05.960
Oh, by any chance, is this the first time
I properly introduced myself?

16:06.330 --> 16:11.580
Uh, well, yes. I am surprised.
I thought you were more of an adult.

16:11.880 --> 16:14.540
Now, come on, that is why I told you, you know?

16:14.540 --> 16:18.130
I said that up until a little while ago,
I was still a little child.

16:18.540 --> 16:23.670
Well, compared to you, Sajo-san,
I probably may still be very much a child, but...

16:25.000 --> 16:27.040
You can do it! You can do it!

16:27.330 --> 16:29.080
Hip, hip, hooray!

16:30.880 --> 16:33.960
Middle school girls these days are seriously impressive!

16:35.500 --> 16:41.460
Sasaki-san, I'm sorry. I've kept you waiting.
I didn't expect it would be this difficult.

16:41.670 --> 16:44.330
Not at all. I am having fun, so it is all right.

16:44.710 --> 16:45.630
An angel...

16:46.130 --> 16:47.750
Um, Sajo-san?

16:48.040 --> 16:48.710
Yes!

16:49.170 --> 16:52.500
About that talk from earlier, but, after all...

16:52.920 --> 16:54.580
Huh? Is something wrong?

16:55.040 --> 16:59.330
Sajo-san, you have already given up
on being with that person, right?

17:00.130 --> 17:01.880
Well, I guess so.

17:02.330 --> 17:04.630
For someone that you have given up on...

17:04.960 --> 17:07.380
Why are you able to do your best to that extent?

17:09.040 --> 17:10.670
That is true, for sure.

17:11.500 --> 17:15.580
But strangely enough, if I think it's for
that person's sake, then I can do my best.

17:18.290 --> 17:22.250
Oh, but Sasaki-san, maybe when you also
fall in love, you'll understand, you know?

17:22.330 --> 17:24.250
M-me? "Fall in love"!?

17:26.080 --> 17:29.630
U-um... What kind of thing is "love"?

17:29.960 --> 17:34.290
Well... As for me, it's not
a particularly fun thing, maybe?

17:34.500 --> 17:36.290
What!? Is that how it is?

17:36.630 --> 17:40.000
Yeah. As for "what is love?", it's more
like I'm the one who wants to know.

17:40.960 --> 17:43.880
Although two and a half years have passed
while I've continued to search for an answer.

17:43.880 --> 17:45.460
I still haven't found it yet.

17:47.920 --> 17:48.670
What's up?

17:48.670 --> 17:49.500
Well...

17:49.670 --> 17:53.750
After having heard my story, did you think if
that's the case, then it'd be better not to fall in love?

17:53.960 --> 17:55.380
Th-that's not...

17:55.830 --> 17:59.000
Although mine is an unrequited love,
it's not all just suffering.

18:00.710 --> 18:04.880
If I didn't have this love, then I think
I would've stayed more like a child.

18:05.420 --> 18:07.540
Is that so...?

18:12.960 --> 18:14.290
Hello!

18:14.630 --> 18:15.420
Huh?

18:15.630 --> 18:18.710
I'm sorry. The craftwork is over for today.

18:19.170 --> 18:23.250
Oops. Is that so? That's too bad. So, she says, Ai-chan.

18:23.500 --> 18:24.960
Let's come again another time.

18:24.960 --> 18:28.330
Thank you. If you'd like to,
please look around at everything.

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>How about making</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>a bracelet that's</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>prefect for you?</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>These are the</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>most popular.</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>Bracelet parts</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>Semi-precious</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:31.710
<b>stones & shells.</b>

18:31.830 --> 18:34.630
Wow, that's cute. So, you can make stuff like this?

18:34.630 --> 18:35.830
Pretty...

18:35.830 --> 18:36.880
Aw...

18:37.670 --> 18:38.580
Huh?

18:47.460 --> 18:48.960
Wow...

18:52.710 --> 18:53.380
Oh!

18:53.580 --> 18:55.580
Aw! Not yet!?

18:55.580 --> 18:57.790
Let's wait just a little bit more, okay?

19:00.920 --> 19:02.380
It couldn't have been...

19:03.960 --> 19:05.380
Aichi, here!

19:05.380 --> 19:06.000
Oh!

19:06.500 --> 19:07.330
Thanks.

19:07.330 --> 19:08.130
Yeah.

19:08.130 --> 19:09.500
Where's Airi's!?

19:09.790 --> 19:11.500
For Ai-chan...

19:11.500 --> 19:13.170
The Kid's Special!

19:11.500 --> 19:14.500
<b>ICE</b>

19:13.170 --> 19:14.250
Yay!

19:14.630 --> 19:17.000
Awesome. Aren't you lucky.

19:17.000 --> 19:17.960
And you, Kei?

19:19.460 --> 19:22.080
The Super Special Tropical Deluxe.

19:22.080 --> 19:22.830
What?

19:23.130 --> 19:25.170
Just kidding. Let's all eat this together.

19:25.250 --> 19:28.000
<b>ICE</b>

19:26.750 --> 19:28.000
It's cold!

19:28.460 --> 19:31.750
Wow! There was even a pineapple here.
Ai-chan, you wanna eat it?

19:31.750 --> 19:32.710
I'll eat it!

19:33.710 --> 19:35.130
Aichi, what's up?

19:35.580 --> 19:39.250
Oh, nothing. I just thought someone
who looked like you-know-who was there, and...

19:39.250 --> 19:40.080
Uh-huh...

19:40.500 --> 19:42.960
That Sajotchi. Even though
we took the effort to invite him.

19:43.420 --> 19:45.790
That he's not here today of all days;
it's like he's missing out.

19:46.210 --> 19:47.880
Is he really at his part-time job?

19:48.290 --> 19:50.210
Huh? Like, maybe he's on a date?

19:50.380 --> 19:52.290
Oh! He of all people; there's no way!

19:52.290 --> 19:53.000
Oh no!

19:53.210 --> 19:55.630
Well, Sajotchi is single-mindedly devoted to you, Aichi.

19:55.960 --> 19:56.710
That's...

19:57.170 --> 19:58.460
Big Sis...

19:58.460 --> 19:59.040
Oh!

20:01.460 --> 20:02.500
Oh my.

20:02.830 --> 20:05.080
C'mere. It's okay. It's fine.

20:06.830 --> 20:09.750
Sajo-san, your piece wasn't able to be finished...

20:10.670 --> 20:11.750
I'm sorry.

20:12.080 --> 20:16.580
It's okay. Sasaki-san, I can't possibly
drag you around until it's late.

20:16.580 --> 20:18.880
If only I didn't have a curfew.

20:18.880 --> 20:21.330
Well, no, your dad would get worried.

20:21.880 --> 20:24.290
Let's come here again. For sure!

20:24.960 --> 20:28.580
Yeah, sure. At that time, Sasaki-san,
I'll get you a present.

20:28.960 --> 20:30.290
Really?

20:30.290 --> 20:31.830
Yeah. Also...

20:32.330 --> 20:36.290
I'll give you the highest grade personal
alarm buzzer for your school commute as well.

20:36.670 --> 20:37.330
Huh?

20:38.290 --> 20:39.630
<b>Shiro 01    Shiroma Station</b>

20:46.460 --> 20:47.750
Will I also...

20:47.750 --> 20:48.290
Huh?

20:48.290 --> 20:52.460
When I become a high schooler,
will I also fall in love?

20:52.460 --> 20:53.000
What?

20:53.540 --> 20:55.630
When I think about it, I am a little scared and...

20:57.630 --> 20:59.330
Why are you laughing!?

20:59.330 --> 21:03.710
Oh, no, I'm sorry. You'll be fine. You see, you won't even
have the emotional leeway to be scared.

21:03.880 --> 21:05.420
Is that how it is?

21:05.580 --> 21:11.380
<b>Stopping at next stop.</b>

21:05.580 --> 21:11.380
<b>If you are next</b>

21:05.590 --> 21:11.380
<b>to this button,</b>

21:05.590 --> 21:11.380
<b>please press it for others.</b>

21:05.830 --> 21:07.330
You should look forward to it.

21:08.380 --> 21:11.380
Aw! Just because you're a senpai,
you have the luxury of that leeway.

21:11.540 --> 21:13.880
It's useless to even worry about the timing of it.

21:13.880 --> 21:16.000
There's nothing that you can like prepare for it.

21:16.380 --> 21:17.500
That's the thing about love.

21:17.500 --> 21:18.460
Aw...

21:18.880 --> 21:21.630
The next stop is Wakamatsu. Wakamatsu.

21:18.880 --> 21:21.880
<b>This bus is headed towards Shiroma Station.</b>

21:18.880 --> 21:21.880
<b>We are stopping at Wakamatsu next.</b>

21:25.460 --> 21:28.330
You must be tired. I'll wake you up when we get there.

21:28.830 --> 21:30.290
Maybe...

21:31.580 --> 21:36.380
It's... Nothing...

21:43.750 --> 21:45.670
So, you are definitely a middle schooler.

21:47.130 --> 21:49.130
<b>You have been invited to a group chat.</b>

21:49.500 --> 21:50.630
What's this?

21:50.750 --> 21:52.790
<b>Sajo, Aika, Kei</b>

21:50.750 --> 21:52.790
<b>You like didn't accept our invitation,</b>

21:50.750 --> 21:52.790
<b>so, lucky you!</b>

21:51.000 --> 21:52.580
Lucky you!

21:54.630 --> 21:55.670
What the!?

21:57.000 --> 22:00.630
What is this!? Why is she in a swimsuit!?
On top of that, this is Mishirohama, right?

22:00.630 --> 22:01.670
Huh!? What!?

22:01.960 --> 22:03.540
Sajo-san...

22:06.540 --> 22:07.330
Oh!

22:08.580 --> 22:09.880
Seriously...?

22:28.580 --> 22:31.040
So annoying! Or so it seems, right?

22:31.330 --> 22:34.630
Aw! I wish I hadn't said that...

22:35.460 --> 22:41.580
But you know, why're you suddenly making
that curt face towards me...?

22:43.290 --> 22:45.500
A text that's been left on read and abandoned

22:45.500 --> 22:47.790
But there are replies if it’s a group text, kind of thing

22:48.000 --> 22:49.960
I thought we were close, but then you became distant

22:50.210 --> 22:51.750
Why am I this lonely?

22:51.750 --> 22:53.630
You're not going to chase after me, today?

22:53.630 --> 22:55.170
I wish I could be honest with myself

22:56.630 --> 23:02.960
That's because it's the first time
I learned there's such a heartrending feeling...

23:02.960 --> 23:04.380
And yet, hey!

23:04.380 --> 23:05.920
Why're you going away??

23:05.920 --> 23:07.670
Why is it a secret!?

23:07.880 --> 23:10.040
I'm full of frustration and...

23:10.040 --> 23:11.420
Oh! Oh!

23:11.420 --> 23:13.130
I can't say something like this

23:13.130 --> 23:17.130
But earlier those weren't my true feelings

23:17.130 --> 23:18.500
Let that get through to you

23:18.580 --> 23:20.210
Why do I get angry...?

23:20.210 --> 23:21.750
I can't be cute...

23:21.750 --> 23:24.210
You don't like me anymore...??

23:24.380 --> 23:27.080
Oh! Oh! Oh, oh!

23:29.080 --> 23:30.040
Why?

23:30.710 --> 23:32.000
Don't hate me

23:35.040 --> 23:36.420
...Listen, "You see...!"
